 "cues": [
  {
   "s": 0.5,
   "e": 2.608,
   "text": "So here's a pretty normal DeFi request."
  },
  {
   "s": 2.648,
   "e": 6.915,
   "text": "Stake five ETH with Lido, use that as collateral on Aave,"
  },
  {
   "s": 6.955,
   "e": 9.272,
   "text": "and borrow a thousand USDC."
  },
  {
   "s": 9.312,
   "e": 12.523,
   "text": "And the same thing on Solana: stake SOL with Marinade,"
  },
  {
   "s": 12.563,
   "e": 17.475,
   "text": "post the mSOL on Kamino, and borrow a thousand USDC."
  },
  {
   "s": 19.525,
   "e": 22.411,
   "text": "On the left is Claude Code with no harness."
  },
  {
   "s": 22.451,
   "e": 25.905,
   "text": "It has to go find the contract addresses, fetch the ABIs,"
  },
  {
   "s": 25.945,
   "e": 29.539,
   "text": "ask you for an RPC endpoint, and write its own script."
  },
  {
   "s": 29.579,
   "e": 32.233,
   "text": "Then it hits a revert, error 27,"
  },
  {
   "s": 32.273,
   "e": 37.876,
   "text": "because Aave actually takes wstETH, not stETH."
  },
  {
   "s": 37.916,
   "e": 41.405,
   "text": "And then it asks for your private key in a .env file."
  },
  {
   "s": 41.445,
   "e": 44.424,
   "text": "On the right it's the same model, through Aomi."
  },
  {
   "s": 44.464,
   "e": 46.851,
   "text": "It reads the wrap rate, simulates the stake,"
  },
  {
   "s": 46.891,
   "e": 48.116,
   "text": "checks the loan-to-value,"
  },
  {
   "s": 48.156,
   "e": 52.012,
   "text": "and all six steps pass on a fork as one bundle."
  },
  {
   "s": 52.562,
   "e": 55.924,
   "text": "Solana is the same story, just with different failures."
  },
  {
   "s": 55.964,
   "e": 59,
   "text": "Claude gets rate-limited on the public RPC,"
  },
  {
   "s": 59.04,
   "e": 61.566,
   "text": "forgets the mSOL token account,"
  },
  {
   "s": 61.606,
   "e": 63.749,
   "text": "misses Kamino's refresh instructions,"
  },
  {
   "s": 63.789,
   "e": 66.314,
   "text": "and then hits the transaction size limit."
  },
  {
   "s": 66.354,
   "e": 68.659,
   "text": "Aomi already knows those accounts and rules,"
  },
  {
   "s": 68.699,
   "e": 71.039,
   "text": "so it simulates everything in LiteSVM and"
  },
  {
   "s": 71.079,
   "e": 73.856,
   "text": "packs it into one versioned transaction."
  },
  {
   "s": 74.107,
   "e": 75.449,
   "text": "Same model, same request."
  },
  {
   "s": 75.489,
   "e": 77.178,
   "text": "The difference is basically how much"
  },
  {
   "s": 77.218,
   "e": 79.612,
   "text": "work the model has to do by itself."
  },
  {
   "s": 79.862,
   "e": 81.726,
   "text": "That's what an execution harness is."
  },
  {
   "s": 81.766,
   "e": 84.71,
   "text": "It's the loop around the model: it gets the context,"
  },
  {
   "s": 84.75,
   "e": 86.416,
   "text": "builds the call, simulates it,"
  },
  {
   "s": 86.456,
   "e": 88.634,
   "text": "and only then commits to your wallet."
  },
  {
   "s": 88.674,
   "e": 90.805,
   "text": "And if something fails, it goes back,"
  },
  {
   "s": 90.845,
   "e": 93.262,
   "text": "reads again, and fixes the call."
  },
  {
   "s": 93.712,
   "e": 96.087,
   "text": "First, context instantiation."
  },
  {
   "s": 96.127,
   "e": 99.222,
   "text": "Reading chain state and wallet state is deterministic,"
  },
  {
   "s": 99.262,
   "e": 100.94,
   "text": "so it doesn't need intelligence."
  },
  {
   "s": 100.98,
   "e": 103.935,
   "text": "It can basically be shrunk to a software function."
  },
  {
   "s": 103.975,
   "e": 106.64,
   "text": "Aomi runs its own nodes and keeps a database"
  },
  {
   "s": 106.68,
   "e": 109.404,
   "text": "of verified contracts and Solana programs,"
  },
  {
   "s": 109.444,
   "e": 110.994,
   "text": "so what took Claude a dozen"
  },
  {
   "s": 111.034,
   "e": 113.845,
   "text": "calls is one call for the model."
  },
  {
   "s": 114.095,
   "e": 115.959,
   "text": "Then transaction construction."
  },
  {
   "s": 115.999,
   "e": 117.77,
   "text": "The model just says what to call."
  },
  {
   "s": 117.81,
   "e": 119.036,
   "text": "The harness builds the bytes,"
  },
  {
   "s": 119.076,
   "e": 121.636,
   "text": "and its protocol skills already know the rules,"
  },
  {
   "s": 121.676,
   "e": 124.028,
   "text": "like Aave wanting wstETH,"
  },
  {
   "s": 124.068,
   "e": 126.687,
   "text": "or Kamino needing a reserve refresh."
  },
  {
   "s": 126.727,
   "e": 129.352,
   "text": "Those are the things Claude had to learn by failing."
  },
  {
   "s": 132.802,
   "e": 134.782,
   "text": "Those same failures still happen here,"
  },
  {
   "s": 134.822,
   "e": 138.493,
   "text": "but they happen on a fork, before anything is sent."
  },
  {
   "s": 140.143,
   "e": 143.342,
   "text": "Every call runs against a fork of live state first."
  },
  {
   "s": 143.382,
   "e": 144.19,
   "text": "When it reverts,"
  },
  {
   "s": 144.23,
   "e": 147.034,
   "text": "the error comes back to the model as back pressure,"
  },
  {
   "s": 147.074,
   "e": 149.646,
   "text": "and only a green run gets committed."
  },
  {
   "s": 149.686,
   "e": 152.804,
   "text": "It's the same idea as CI for coding agents:"
  },
  {
   "s": 152.844,
   "e": 154.952,
   "text": "tests push back when something breaks,"
  },
  {
   "s": 154.992,
   "e": 157.35,
   "text": "so the model writes good code."
  },
  {
   "s": 162.001,
   "e": 163.25,
   "text": "Once everything passes,"
  },
  {
   "s": 163.29,
   "e": 167,
   "text": "Aomi compresses the whole sequence into one transaction."
  },
  {
   "s": 167.04,
   "e": 168.881,
   "text": "On Ethereum that's a smart wallet"
  },
  {
   "s": 168.921,
   "e": 170.75,
   "text": "bundle with account abstraction,"
  },
  {
   "s": 170.79,
   "e": 172.642,
   "text": "and on Solana it's one versioned"
  },
  {
   "s": 172.682,
   "e": 174.86,
   "text": "transaction with a lookup table."
  },
  {
   "s": 174.9,
   "e": 178.261,
   "text": "The harness does this to save gas and settlement time."
  },
  {
   "s": 178.301,
   "e": 182.227,
   "text": "Compressing deterministic work means the model does less."
  },
  {
   "s": 182.477,
   "e": 184.701,
   "text": "And the key never goes to the model."
  },
  {
   "s": 184.741,
   "e": 187.58,
   "text": "Commit hands your wallet a signable transaction,"
  },
  {
   "s": 187.62,
   "e": 188.428,
   "text": "and you sign it,"
  },
  {
   "s": 188.468,
   "e": 191.144,
   "text": "or a scoped session or an agent wallet"
  },
  {
   "s": 191.184,
   "e": 193.176,
   "text": "signs within the limits you set."
  },
  {
   "s": 193.216,
   "e": 197.642,
   "text": "On Solana, a Swig role enforces those limits onchain."
  },
  {
   "s": 199.892,
   "e": 203.679,
   "text": "Then the chain settles it, like any other transaction."
  },
  {
   "s": 206.329,
   "e": 208.983,
   "text": "After that, Aomi checks the onchain result"
  },
  {
   "s": 209.023,
   "e": 210.91,
   "text": "against the simulation you approved,"
  },
  {
   "s": 210.95,
   "e": 213.917,
   "text": "and keeps one record from instruction to receipt."
  },
  {
   "s": 213.957,
   "e": 216.448,
   "text": "Claude's version ends with check Etherscan."
  },
  {
   "s": 216.488,
   "e": 219.914,
   "text": "This is the part a fund actually needs to audit."
  },
  {
   "s": 220.365,
   "e": 222.34,
   "text": "So, same model, same request."
  },
  {
   "s": 222.79,
   "e": 224.596,
   "text": "The model interprets the intent,"
  },
  {
   "s": 224.636,
   "e": 225.954,
   "text": "your wallet holds the key,"
  },
  {
   "s": 225.994,
   "e": 229.27,
   "text": "and Aomi facilitates everything in between."
  }
 ],
